2026-11-19 19:41:18 - Agent_20261119193803 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed all 19 results from query 20261119192950 (py/pillow-xml-context). All 19 results point into a single function, PIL.Image.Image.getexif() (src/PIL/Image.py, ~1286-1316); the reported `Attribute()`/`range()`/`tuple()`/`int()` locations are merely attribute accesses along the same code path, not independent sinks. There is exactly one XML parsing sink: `xml.etree.ElementTree.fromstring(xmp_tags)` at line 1309, where `xmp_tags` comes from untrusted image metadata `self.info["XML:com.adobe.xmp"]` (attacker-controlled XMP packet embedded in PNG/JPEG/WebP files). Pillow's stdlib ElementTree parser expands internal entities and supports DTDs, so a crafted XMP packet can trigger billion-laughs / quadratic-blowup entity expansion (CWE-776) and, via external entity resolution in some configurations, XXE-style disclosure (CWE-611). WebPImagePlugin.py:91 stores the raw XMP chunk into `info["xmp"]`, confirming image-derived XMP reaches this sink. Submitted 1 true-positive finding for the confirmed sink (src/PIL/Image.py:1309). No separate additional vulnerabilities were identified; the XMP *writing* paths (WebPImagePlugin encode) and the many test-file hits are not exploitable.
